usb_bluetooth License

Copyright (c) 2024-2026 youkorr

usb_bluetooth is the Bluetooth component of Portall, from
https://github.com/youkorr/esphome_esp-video, published as a folder of its
own. Its code -- the Python configuration and codegen, the C++ and the CMake
in components/usb_bluetooth/ -- is licensed under the MIT License below. Every
source file says so in an SPDX header.

What is NOT covered by this licence:

  - components/usb_bluetooth/firmware/rtl8761bu_fw.bin and
    rtl8761bu_config.bin are Realtek's, from linux-firmware, unmodified, and
    redistributed under Realtek's own licence: LICENCE.rtlwifi_firmware.txt
    beside them, which must go with them.
  - CherryUSB (Apache-2.0) is downloaded when a firmware is built, not
    carried here; cherryusb_patch changes one constant in that downloaded
    copy.
  - With `transport: idf`, the USB layer in idf_usb.h and idf_usb.cpp is
    this component's own and is MIT like the rest; the USB Host Library it
    calls is Espressif's (Apache-2.0), part of ESP-IDF 5.5 or downloaded as
    espressif/usb on ESP-IDF 6, and is not carried here.
  - The component builds on ESPHome (Python under MIT, C++ under GPLv3) and
    ESP-IDF (Apache-2.0). A firmware compiled with it is a combined work and
    is, as a whole, subject to their terms as well.

Some numbers in the code were found by reading Linux's Bluetooth drivers
(GPL-2.0) and bluepad32 (Apache-2.0); none of their code is here. The NOTICE
file of the main repository lists them.

